From: VLCDotNet CI <ci@vlcdotnet>
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec: define FF_PROFILE_AV1_* fallbacks for newer FFmpeg

The prebuilt VLC contribs (used for the Windows/Apple/Android builds) ship a
newer FFmpeg where the FF_PROFILE_AV1_MAIN / FF_PROFILE_AV1_HIGH /
FF_PROFILE_AV1_PROFESSIONAL aliases were dropped in favour of AV_PROFILE_*.
VLC 3.0.23's AVPROFILE() still selects the FF_PROFILE_* spelling for some
libavcodec versions, so modules/codec/avcodec/directx_va.c fails to compile
with "FF_PROFILE_AV1_MAIN undeclared".

Provide fallback definitions guarded by #ifndef. The AV1 profile values are
stable (main=0, high=1, professional=2), and where the symbols already exist
(e.g. the from-source Linux FFmpeg) the guards make this a no-op.
---
 modules/codec/avcodec/avcommon_compat.h | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/codec/avcodec/avcommon_compat.h b/modules/codec/avcodec/avcommon_compat.h
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/modules/codec/avcodec/avcommon_compat.h
+++ b/modules/codec/avcodec/avcommon_compat.h
@@ -37,6 +37,17 @@
 #ifdef HAVE_LIBAVCODEC_AVCODEC_H
 #include <libavcodec/avcodec.h>
 
+/* Newer FFmpeg drops the FF_PROFILE_AV1_* aliases used by VLC's pre-AV_PROFILE
+ * code path. Provide fallbacks; AV1 profile values are stable (0/1/2). */
+#ifndef FF_PROFILE_AV1_MAIN
+# define FF_PROFILE_AV1_MAIN 0
+#endif
+#ifndef FF_PROFILE_AV1_HIGH
+# define FF_PROFILE_AV1_HIGH 1
+#endif
+#ifndef FF_PROFILE_AV1_PROFESSIONAL
+# define FF_PROFILE_AV1_PROFESSIONAL 2
+#endif
+
 /* check the FFmpeg libavutil version */
 #define LIBAVCODEC_VERSION_CHECK( a, d, e ) \
